  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Frosted Sugar Cookie Blizzard — Holiday Baking in a Cup</h2>
  <p>The Frosted Sugar Cookie Blizzard captures the essence of holiday sugar cookies — the buttery, vanilla-sweet cookie itself plus the characteristic pink or white frosting. In DQ soft serve, it becomes a rich, sweet, cake-adjacent Blizzard that is distinct from the chocolate-heavy options that dominate the year-round lineup. Find all current Blizzard flavors on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

  <h2>Frosted Sugar Cookie vs. Confetti Cake Blizzard</h2>
  <p>Both Blizzards are in the "baked goods" flavor category. The key differences:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Frosted Sugar Cookie</strong> — Sugar cookie pieces with frosting. A more buttery, vanilla-cookie flavor. Holiday seasonal.</li>
    <li><a href="/items/confetti-cake-blizzard"><strong>Confetti Cake Blizzard</strong></a> — Cake pieces with rainbow sprinkles. More birthday-cake adjacent, brighter flavor. Summer seasonal.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Both are sweet, dessert-forward Blizzards without chocolate or peanut butter — the right choice for guests who prefer lighter flavor profiles.</p>

  <h2>Who Should Order the Frosted Sugar Cookie Blizzard</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Holiday season dessert seekers</strong> — A festive, on-theme dessert for November and December visits</li>
    <li><strong>Guests who prefer sweet over chocolate</strong> — The Frosted Sugar Cookie is sweet without any chocolate intensity</li>
    <li><strong>Kids and families</strong> — The familiar sugar cookie flavor is broadly appealing to younger guests</li>
    <li><strong>Guests who want something light</strong> — At ~510 cal Small, it is mid-range for Blizzard calories</li>
  </ul>

